      "label": "Numbers With Units",
      "excerpt": "Coherence first. What exists: Star Wars's own to measure (amount) in (unit) acti",
      "text": "Create the base `dimensions` class in TS, then the actual unit files in spell.\n\nSomething like `\nlength is a dimension:\n  - its base is \"meters\", aka \"m\"\n  - one \"centimeter\", aka \"cm\", is 1/100 m\n  - one \"inch', aka \"in\", aka '\"', is 2.54cm\n```",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T01:21:07.076Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Dimensions",
      "offset": 317,
      "edited": "2026-11-04T01:24:24.242Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T01:31:27.221Z",
          "html": "<p>Done in P23's plan:  a <code>Dimension</code> base class in the TypeScript core (and Python's), and each built-in dimension written in Spell, in your shape:</p>\n<pre>length is a dimension:\n  - its base is \"meter\", aka \"m\"\n  - one \"centimeter\", aka \"cm\", is 1/100 m\n  - one \"inch\", aka \"in\", aka '\"', is 2.54 cm</pre>\n<p>A program declares its own the same way.  Temperature needs a starting point as well as a factor (32 °F is 0 °C):  that's Q39, recommending <code>is 5/9 °C, starting at 32</code>.  The plan waits for your Accept again.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-04T01:29:58.515Z"
      }
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "p-app-themes-in-spell#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "App Themes in Spell",
      "excerpt": "An app says its widget defaults in Spell, in a <theme> block (spellml) or its th",
      "text": "don't need `<theme>` block, <ui-defaults> is more generic",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-04T01:28:38.613Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "<theme>",
      "offset": 47,
      "edited": "2026-11-04T01:28:39.604Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-04T01:31:28.197Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  no <code>&lt;theme&gt;</code> block or <code>its theme:</code> lines.  <code>&lt;ui-defaults&gt;</code>, inline or with <code>source=</code>, is the one form in P29's goal, changes and plan.  It waits for your Accept again.</p>"
        }
      ],
